; Disassembly of Digicool Things' 8-bit_oled_thing_v1.1.s19: the 8-bit OLED Thing v1.1's factory firmware.
; Digicool's work, here with Greg's permission; not covered by Wren's MIT licence.
;
; Compiled C (an ST Visual Develop "Release" build, Cosmic's .sm8 output) with ST's Standard
; Peripheral Library linked in. Disassembled with ucsim 0.6.4 (sstm8) by following the code
; from the interrupt vectors through every call, jump and branch; code nothing reaches is
; decoded too and marked "never called"; tables are shown as bytes. Register names are from
; firmware/include/stm8s003.inc. The comments come from reading the code and running the
; image in Wren's emulator; docs/OledThing.md describes the behaviour.

; ---- Interrupt vectors ----
    8000  82 00 8C CB    int    reset                   ; reset
    8004  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; TRAP
    8008  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 0
    800C  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 1
    8010  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 2
    8014  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 3
    8018  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 4
    801C  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 5
    8020  82 00 8F 3D    int    exti_port_d             ; IRQ 6
    8024  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 7
    8028  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 8
    802C  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 9
    8030  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 10
    8034  82 00 9E 7D    int    unused_irq              ; IRQ 11
